
Document 1 — Phase 1 Technical Summary
1. Purpose
Phase 1 builds the electromagnetic kernel for the layered-medium Method of Moments (MoM) — the same class of solver as CST's HF Multilayer. The kernel is the mixed-potential Green's function of the air / LiNbO₃ / SiO₂ / Si / air stack, evaluated at the metal plane. Two kernels are needed:

G_q(ρ) — scalar-potential (charge) kernel, enters the ∇·J term of the MPIE.

G_A(ρ) — vector-potential (current) kernel, enters the jωA term.

Both depend only on the stack and the frequency, not on the metal geometry. That is the point of the layered-medium approach: the stack is solved once as a canonical problem, then reused for every geometry via matrix assembly.

